{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854746-caern-raiding","id":854746,"title":"Caern Raiding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-28T17:34:42-07:00","id":854746,"title":"Caern Raiding","content":"Can other 'races' of the WoD make use of the spiritual energies of a Garou Caern?<br /> I would imagine Mages could do it.<br /> But, are there any Thaumaturgical Paths which could do anything interesting/useful with a conquered or abandoned Caern?<br /> What about Changelings? <br /> Or are the various 'energies' of the world too different to be used by one another?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T17:38:55-07:00","id":854748,"title":"","content":"Mages theoretically can but doing is another matter. The technocracy is more then likely to &quot;sanitize&quot; the node, I.e drain it for all its worth and build a strip mall over it.<br /> <br /> Vampires not so much, thaum is powered by blood.<br /> <br /> I could see some changelings setting up shop in an abandoned Caren but not raiding one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T22:19:58-07:00","id":854881,"title":"","content":"Mages trying to do so is a major reason why the Garou and Fera tend to tear mages apart on sight, provided they know what they're dealing with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T03:17:06-07:00","id":854963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854746-caern-raiding#post854746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can other 'races' of the WoD make use of the spiritual energies of a Garou Caern?<br /> I would imagine Mages could do it.<br /> But, are there any Thaumaturgical Paths which could do anything interesting/useful with a conquered or abandoned Caern?<br /> What about Changelings?<br /> Or are the various 'energies' of the world too different to be used by one another?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lhiannan can destroy or maybe use it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","user":"Rettile&amp;Blitch","date":". 03-29-2016, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T09:33:50-07:00","id":855115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854746-caern-raiding#post854746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can other 'races' of the WoD make use of the spiritual energies of a Garou Caern?<br /> I would imagine Mages could do it.<br /> But, are there any Thaumaturgical Paths which could do anything interesting/useful with a conquered or abandoned Caern?<br /> What about Changelings?<br /> Or are the various 'energies' of the world too different to be used by one another?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tass is tass is tass. Glamour and Vitae are specific forms of tass, so anything that required them specifically would not work on Gnosis, but anything a Mage would want it to do would work just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:19:15-07:00","id":856524,"title":"","content":"the Lhinian from the Dark ages could use a Caern though it would set the Garou on them like sharks on blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:49:04-07:00","id":856546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854746-caern-raiding?p=856524#post856524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Lhinian from the Dark ages could use a Caern though it would set the Garou on them like sharks on blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because their magic always brought in banes, never anything pure. That's the only thing that answers the call of the undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:12:44-07:00","id":856679,"title":"","content":"Didn't the KotE do something with Caerns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:38:44-07:00","id":856694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854746-caern-raiding?p=856679#post856679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the KotE do something with Caerns?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have some funky geomancy stuff, technically a dragon nest is a node/caern","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:24:24-07:00","id":856861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854746-caern-raiding?p=856694#post856694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have some funky geomancy stuff, technically a dragon nest is a node/caern</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they do pretty much everything with caerns that Garou and Fera do. Their taste for purity, oddly enough, makes the Hungry Dead more inclined to care after said manifestations of purity, making for... strange relationships between courts of Ferocious People and Hungry Dead. Devil-Tigers are typically a notable exception, unless they've consistently picked up the devil and realized that being one is much more like being Gene Wilder's Willy Wonka (to the point that one of the sigs for the Dharma is, in fact, basically undead Japanese Willy Wonka) than a cannibal rapist edgelord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T00:54:17-07:00","id":857011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854746-caern-raiding?p=856861#post856861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, they do pretty much everything with caerns that Garou and Fera do. Their taste for purity, oddly enough, makes the Hungry Dead more inclined to care after said manifestations of purity, making for... strange relationships between courts of Ferocious People and Hungry Dead. Devil-Tigers are typically a notable exception, unless they've consistently picked up the devil and realized that being one is much more like being Gene Wilder's Willy Wonka (to the point that one of the sigs for the Dharma is, in fact, basically undead Japanese Willy Wonka) than a cannibal rapist edgelord.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found the Devil Tiger Dharmabook utterly amazing. As presented in the core they are either grimdark rapist edgelords or blood knights. In the Dharma book you realise they are utterly inhuman, and that there is a point to their madness, and that pointless random acts of cruelty are beneath them as they teach nothing. That book still gives me warm fuzzy feelings :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}